WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.497
Warning! Warning!

2
00:00:01.497 --> 00:00:06.705
I built this with AI and text to speech, because I can't narrate for shit!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.359
Hey, Dreamer here.

4
00:00:09.359 --> 00:00:15.026
The world's got people now, so let's sort out the most important one: the player.

5
00:00:15.026 --> 00:00:18.734
Premade characters, random names, character creation,

6
00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:22.022
and a filter for names the AI won't stop using.

7
00:00:23.433 --> 00:00:27.212
Open Characters, then Player Character, then Premade Characters.

8
00:00:27.212 --> 00:00:31.877
These are ready-made characters players can pick instead of building their own.

9
00:00:31.877 --> 00:00:37.191
We've got two new acts, Jack Tumble the escape artist and Nell Bramwell the knife thrower.

10
00:00:37.633 --> 00:00:43.338
The description is what players read when they pick, and the story uses it as their background.

11
00:00:43.338 --> 00:00:45.319
Open with a hook that sells them.

12
00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:50.512
Traits are where a premade gets its stats, skills, moves and starting gear.

13
00:00:50.512 --> 00:00:54.434
Ours are empty for now, because we build traits in season two.

14
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.011
And a voice tag, same as for people.

15
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:05.726
Random Character Names is the list Voyage draws from when it picks a name for a character.

16
00:01:05.726 --> 00:01:11.138
Its own list is very fantasy, so ours is country-fair names, surname and all.

17
00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.442
One list for men, one for women.

18
00:01:14.442 --> 00:01:18.705
Keep at least ten in each so names don't repeat.

19
00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.831
Character Creation has one switch here.

20
00:01:22.831 --> 00:01:27.173
Turned on, a player who picks a premade can still change them.

21
00:01:27.173 --> 00:01:31.234
Turned off, they play the premade exactly as you wrote it.

22
00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:35.829
And Name Filter Settings, under Characters.

23
00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:41.329
Every entry is a name the AI reaches for too often, like Marcus and Elara.

24
00:01:41.767 --> 00:01:45.745
When it comes up with one, it swaps in a replacement from the list.

25
00:01:45.745 --> 00:01:49.544
Voyage's replacements for Elara were things like Nova and Astra,

26
00:01:49.544 --> 00:01:52.810
so I swapped them for names that fit our country towns.

27
00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.838
Keep it to names: it isn't built for banning words.

28
00:01:57.233 --> 00:01:58.898
That's the player sorted.

29
00:01:58.898 --> 00:02:02.428
Our premades and names are linked in the description.

30
00:02:02.428 --> 00:02:09.087
Next time, the last one of the season: game start, where everything we've built finally gets played.

31
00:02:09.533 --> 00:02:13.481
I'm Dreamer. Now go build something weird, and I'll see you next time!

